ARRAY LIST: ArrayList is a resizable array implementation of the List interface
            found in the Java Collections Framework.

Unlike a normal array, an ArrayList can grow or shrink dynamically as elements are added or removed.

Method	Description
add(element)	Adds an element
get(index)	Retrieves an element
set(index, element)	Replaces an element
remove(index)	Removes an element
size()	Returns the number of elements
contains(element)	Checks if an element exists
clear()	Removes all elements

ArrayList<String> names = new ArrayList<>();
ArrayList<Integer> ages = new ArrayList<>();


